1. Aim
To write a Python program to demonstrate Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts using classes, objects, and inheritance.

2. Algorithm
Start the program.

Create a parent class named Person.

Define a constructor to initialize the name and age.

Create a method to display the person's details.

Create a child class named Student that inherits the Person class.

Add a constructor to initialize the roll number and course.

Use the super() function to call the parent class constructor.

Create an object of the Student class.

Display the student details using the object.

Stop the program.
